<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<resources>
    <!--
      The diameter of the mark's disc on the surfaces this project sizes
      itself: the pre-31 launch window and the recents card, both drawn from
      `contour_splash.xml`.

      112 is `MarkTile`'s size and the lock screen's. It is deliberately *not*
      the size of the Android 12 splash icon, which is not ours to choose —
      Android renders that at its own canvas size, measured at 188dp on a
      Galaxy S24. `SPLASH_DISC_PX` in `packages/ui/src/lock-timing.ts` carries
      that number and the app's own splash matches it.

      The disc's share of the adaptive icon and the mark's share of each disc
      are no longer dimens: they live inside the generated vectors, as
      proportions of a viewport, because a dp declared in a layer-list is not
      honoured when Android scales a drawable to fill a canvas. That is exactly
      how the splash disc ended up two thirds too large.
    -->
    <dimen name="contour_mark_disc">112dp</dimen>

    <!--
      The box `contour_splash.xml` draws the splash vector in.

      Not 112, even though the disc that comes out of it is. That vector carries
      an invisible ground circle filling its viewport, which is the trick that
      makes the disc's size ours to choose at all — so the file is 288 wide to
      yield a 112 disc, and asking for 112 here would produce a 44dp one.

      288 is Android's own splash icon canvas, which the vector's viewport
      matches so that its units are dp. See `scripts/generate-icons.mjs`.
    -->
    <dimen name="splash_icon_box">288dp</dimen>
</resources>
